Conclusion and Recommendations
Question 17: What are your conclusions from the analysis? What recommendations would you like to share to help improve the business? (You can use cuisine type and feedback ratings to drive your business recommendations.) [6 marks]
Conclusions:

    The dataset contains 1,898 orders across 178 restaurants and 14 cuisine types.
    Demand is concentrated on weekends, which account for about 71% of all orders.
    The most ordered cuisines are American, Japanese, Italian, and Chinese.
    Shake Shack, The Meatball Shop, Blue Ribbon Sushi, Blue Ribbon Fried Chicken, and Parm are the top restaurants by order volume.
    The average food preparation time is about 27.37 minutes, and the average delivery time is about 24.16 minutes.
    Weekday deliveries are slower than weekend deliveries, with an average of 28.34 minutes compared with 22.47 minutes on weekends.
    About 29.24% of orders cost more than $20, and these orders are important because they generate higher commission revenue.
    The company generated approximately $6,166.30 in net commission revenue from the orders in this dataset.
    A large number of orders, 736, were not rated, which limits the usefulness of customer feedback analysis.

Recommendations:

    Prioritize partnerships, promotions, and app placement for high-volume cuisines, especially American, Japanese, Italian, and Chinese, because these categories drive most demand.
    Offer promotional support to restaurants that meet the rating criteria: The Meatball Shop, Blue Ribbon Fried Chicken, Shake Shack, and Blue Ribbon Sushi.
    Investigate weekday delivery operations because weekday delivery time is meaningfully higher than weekend delivery time. More delivery partners or better routing may be needed during weekday demand peaks.
    Encourage more customers to submit ratings, for example through small loyalty points or post-delivery reminders, because many orders are currently marked Not given.
    Use targeted vouchers for the top frequent customers, especially customer IDs 52832, 47440, 83287, 250494, and 65009, to improve retention.
    Focus upselling and bundled offers around orders near the 20threshold,sinceordersabove

    20 generate the highest commission rate.

